RECOVERY

Check stops bad step before run. Nothing ran. Code kept in `rejected`. Fix by
edit, not rewrite: edit forms change rejected, then fixed code checked and run
as this step.
- (revise :old "text" :new "text") replace text found once. No match or many
  fails: quote more around it.
- (rename old new) rename symbol everywhere. Strings untouched.
- (close-parens) close parens left open, at end of form.
- (add-arg f :key value) add keyword arg to the one call of f.
- (push-arg f value) add positional arg to the one call of f, before its
  keywords.
Each edit works on last failed form of stopped step. Other form: add
:in, whole entry or its form number, e.g.
(rename old new :in (car (failed-forms))).
- (failed-forms) forms check found problems in, last one last. Each alist:
  form (number), line, text, problems. Read field: (get-in f :text).
Edit forms go alone in step, applied in order. Rewrite only when no edit says
it.
